From a52f99efb29f15b7355eef41445d11f927fd3220 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 16:36:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 076/638] [AROS] Omit unsupported renderer malloc extensions

AI_PHASE: Phase 3 - single-process headless shell
AI_STATUS: The renderer thread compiles without a nonstandard allocator header.
ROOT_CAUSE: render_thread_impl included <malloc.h> on every non-Apple platform even though AROS does not provide that extension header and the file consumes none of its declarations.
FIX_REASON: Apply Chromium's existing AROS allocator-header policy and omit an unused platform extension.
SCOPE: content/renderer/render_thread_impl.cc include selection only.
VALIDATION: render_thread_impl.o compiled with the AROS headless toolchain.
RISK: None; the translation unit has no malloc-extension references.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
Continues: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
---
 content/renderer/render_thread_impl.cc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/content/renderer/render_thread_impl.cc b/content/renderer/render_thread_impl.cc
index 3594bc7a25..f61213d979 100644
--- a/content/renderer/render_thread_impl.cc
+++ b/content/renderer/render_thread_impl.cc
@@ -203,7 +203,7 @@
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_APPLE)
 #include <malloc/malloc.h>
-#else
+#elif !BUILDFLAG(IS_AROS)
 #include <malloc.h>
 #endif
 
